## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a practical, browser-based NLP tool with a hybrid model, latency constraints, multilingual support, and privacy.

## Key Concepts

- Hybrid NLP: rule-based cues + lightweight ML
- WebAssembly performance and memory constraints
- Multilingual handling (EN/ES) with minimal data
- Explainability: top cues, confidence

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: simple feature extraction and LR scoring sketch
function score(text, cues){
  let features={};
  cues.forEach(c=>{ features[c] = (text.includes(c))?1:0;});
  // simple logistic regression with fixed weights
  const weights = {cue1:1.2, cue2:-0.9};
  let z = 0;
  for(const k in features){ if(features[k]) z += weights[k]||0; }
  const p = 1/(1+Math.exp(-z));
  return {p, cues: Object.keys(features).filter(k=>features[k])};
}
```

